{
  "requirement_id": "SFMC-REQ-004",
  "raw_text": "When the pilot selects a destination, the SFMC shall calculate a safe and efficient route to the destination.",
  "software_requirement_status": "YES",
  "quality_status": "NEEDS_REVIEW",
  "quality_issues": [
    {
      "issue_code": "UNDEFINED_TERM",
      "severity": "MAJOR",
      "explanation": "The requirement uses the terms \"safe\" and \"efficient route\" without defining what constitutes a safe or efficient route. The SRS explicitly lists \"Definition of a safe route\" as an open item (#1 in section 11), indicating these terms are currently undefined and ambiguous.",
      "srs_evidence": [
        {
          "locator": "11. Open Items",
          "excerpt": "1. Definition of a **safe route**."
        },
        {
          "locator": "3.1 Navigation",
          "excerpt": "SFMC-REQ-004 — Route Calculation\nWhen the pilot selects a destination, the SFMC shall calculate a safe and efficient route to the destination."
        }
      ],
      "nasa_references": [
        {
          "document": "NASA-HDBK-2203-5.09",
          "authority": "HANDBOOK_GUIDANCE",
          "section": "§3.2.1.1.4",
          "swe_id": null,
          "url": "https://swehb.nasa.gov/spaces/SWEHBVD/pages/102695669/5.09+-+SRS+-+Software+Requirements+Specification"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Define the terms \"safe route\" and \"efficient route\" clearly within the SRS or in an associated glossary to remove ambiguity and enable verification and validation.",
      "requires_stakeholder_input": true
    },
    {
      "issue_code": "ALLOCATION_UNCLEAR",
      "severity": "MINOR",
      "explanation": "The requirement states that the SFMC shall calculate the route but does not specify whether this calculation is purely software-based or involves hardware or external subsystem support. The SRS mentions the Navigation System provides position and destination coordinates but does not clarify if route calculation is a software responsibility or shared with Navigation System hardware.",
      "srs_evidence": [
        {
          "locator": "2.2 Navigation System",
          "excerpt": "The Navigation System provides the SFMC with:\n- spacecraft position,\n- spacecraft velocity,\n- spacecraft orientation, and\n- destination coordinates."
        },
        {
          "locator": "3.1 Navigation",
          "excerpt": "SFMC-REQ-004 — Route Calculation\nWhen the pilot selects a destination, the SFMC shall calculate a safe and efficient route to the destination."
        }
      ],
      "nasa_references": [
        {
          "document": "NASA-HDBK-2203-5.09",
          "authority": "HANDBOOK_GUIDANCE",
          "section": "§3.2.1.1.4",
          "swe_id": null,
          "url": "https://swehb.nasa.gov/spaces/SWEHBVD/pages/102695669/5.09+-+SRS+-+Software+Requirements+Specification"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Clarify the software allocation for route calculation, specifying whether the SFMC software alone performs this function or if it relies on other subsystems or hardware components.",
      "requires_stakeholder_input": true
    }
  ],
  "primary_swe_id": null,
  "primary_swe_strength": null,
  "swe_links": [],
  "summary": "The requirement SFMC-REQ-004 is a valid software requirement specifying that the SFMC shall calculate a safe and efficient route upon pilot destination selection. However, it currently lacks definitions for key terms \"safe\" and \"efficient route,\" which are noted as open items in the SRS. Additionally, the software allocation for route calculation is not explicitly stated, leading to some ambiguity. These issues require stakeholder input to resolve. No direct NPR SWE linkage is justified based on the supplied evidence."
}
